#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186605135 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46cb5d30-23a3-5cf8-a0d5-0b9f7450d522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604808} {:answer/id #uuid "48ecc67b-cf3e-5927-a6aa-4c41be0cdbed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+6{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604811} {:answer/id #uuid "9a5f4c98-0dfd-5f3a-84d5-14642fe0403e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{3}{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604891} {:answer/id #uuid "b927fd14-1857-5606-924f-1f3213d4db60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604930} {:answer/id #uuid "d4fd84f0-62bf-51d4-910d-686e4f7bf24e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b927fd14-1857-5606-924f-1f3213d4db60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604930} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a0e129a-ab4c-5d0d-9978-7ed6be98fbf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c4dca02e-edf1-5494-a3ee-03c75dee63c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-113787" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 2x-3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x-3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\right)-3\\left(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\right)+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-{x}^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186610506 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "165ecc04-7fbd-5a77-93f6-d22774668d8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\sqrt{2} e^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610508} {:answer/id #uuid "a9a9eb71-d6f4-5e56-a789-44d48c2f4a4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{2} e^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610522} {:answer/id #uuid "c05b88fb-a1f5-578d-b994-6446f57d9da5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 \\sqrt{2} e^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610523} {:answer/id #uuid "c158e98d-9be1-5924-824f-86a906952603" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2} e^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610524} {:answer/id #uuid "e7d12503-47d7-5f59-a1b1-50b38d30a30b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7d12503-47d7-5f59-a1b1-50b38d30a30b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610530} :answer-field/id #uuid "35cfa76c-d46c-58d5-abac-80705a446e4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610514}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0d6c902f-2435-5203-aa9f-262524ac5a30" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(2 e^{x})\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}),$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=2 e^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\nu'(x)=2 e^{x},\\quad v'(x)=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx} &=uv'(x)+vu'(x) \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(2 e^{x})\\cdot (\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &{}+(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (2 e^{x})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=2 e^{x}(\\cos x+\\sin x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left.\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}\\right|_{x=\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}} &=\\begin{aligned}&(2 e^{\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}\\right)})\\cdot (\\cos{\\left(\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}\\right) \\right)}) \\\\ &{}+(\\sin{\\left(\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}\\right) \\right)})\\cdot (2 e^{\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}\\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(2 e^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}})\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &{}+\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\cdot (2 e^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186610512 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c653dab-d9d6-5b47-ba64-cbbe5b46db95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{e^{\\pi}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610511} {:answer/id #uuid "4113257e-c58c-52bb-ba02-31e91a438929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610515} {:answer/id #uuid "6b30face-c814-5cf8-878a-8e44698640ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 e^{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610518} {:answer/id #uuid "91feb006-6edf-5c92-814e-860c6f6c38e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{e^{\\pi}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610521} {:answer/id #uuid "c9c63d51-a96d-5e42-858d-40ab7b62ab2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- e^{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9c63d51-a96d-5e42-858d-40ab7b62ab2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- e^{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610526} :answer-field/id #uuid "549d2205-841f-52e6-a67c-6b578550ece4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610516}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "30877dff-2142-58cc-a6f0-c31f215bf1ca" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(e^{x})\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}),$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\pi.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=e^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\nu'(x)=e^{x},\\quad v'(x)=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx} &=uv'(x)+vu'(x) \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(e^{x})\\cdot (\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &{}+(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (e^{x})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=e^{x}(\\cos x+\\sin x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\pi$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left.\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}\\right|_{x=\\pi} &=\\begin{aligned}&(e^{(\\pi)})\\cdot (\\cos{\\left((\\pi) \\right)}) \\\\ &{}+(\\sin{\\left((\\pi) \\right)})\\cdot (e^{(\\pi)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(e^{\\pi})\\cdot (-1)+(0)\\cdot (e^{\\pi}) \\\\ &=- e^{\\pi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $- e^{\\pi}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186610517 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0342fedd-8d06-51bf-b9ad-5e63f5f5f982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27 \\pi^{2}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610505} {:answer/id #uuid "173ff202-950a-5940-aabe-82d481b5d461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27 \\pi^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610509} {:answer/id #uuid "c354a2c8-b0de-585b-8ee4-0a43e6df96a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{27 \\pi^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610525} {:answer/id #uuid "cb0129b4-44ea-5647-bf41-eda356ea7056" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{81 \\pi^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610527} {:answer/id #uuid "e16fa939-f833-50c4-9a94-5a392aabfb39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{81 \\pi^{2}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "173ff202-950a-5940-aabe-82d481b5d461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27 \\pi^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610509} :answer-field/id #uuid "f04cda44-d833-5a4f-9cef-56d38d1b0af1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610531}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6996047e-7e31-5564-bb70-e58aabf2bfcd" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(- x^{3})\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}$." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=- x^{3}$ and $v(x)=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\nu'(x)=- 3 x^{2},\\quad v'(x)=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx} &=uv'(x)+vu'(x) \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- x^{3})\\cdot (\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &{}+(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (- 3 x^{2})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=- x^{2} \\left(x \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + 3 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left.\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}\\right|_{x=\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} &=\\begin{aligned}&(- \\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\right)^{3})\\cdot (\\cos{\\left(\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\right) \\right)}) \\\\ &{}+(\\sin{\\left(\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\right) \\right)})\\cdot (- 3 \\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\right)^{2})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(- \\frac{27 \\pi^{3}}{8}\\right)\\cdot (0) \\\\ &{}+(-1)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{27 \\pi^{2}}{4}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\frac{27 \\pi^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $\\frac{27 \\pi^{2}}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186610519 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a49124e-b359-593a-a72b-ef618ed162eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\left(3 - \\pi\\right)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a49124e-b359-593a-a72b-ef618ed162eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\left(3 - \\pi\\right)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610510} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f7d6f26-56ba-523c-91e9-3177f7b66fb2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6ecb8282-6295-5cd9-a5b5-e1bb578640a9" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(4 x + 1)\\cdot (\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}),$ then the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=4 x + 1$ and $v(x)=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\nu'(x)=4,\\quad v'(x)=- \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx} &=uv'(x)+vu'(x) \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(4 x + 1)\\cdot (- \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &{}+(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (4)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=-(4 x + 1)\\sin x+4\\cos x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left.\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}\\right|_{x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}} &=\\begin{aligned}&(4 \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) + 1)\\cdot (- \\sin{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\right)}) \\\\ &{}+(\\cos{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\right)})\\cdot (4)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(1 + \\pi)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &{}+\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\cdot (4)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\left(3 - \\pi\\right)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $\\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\left(3 - \\pi\\right)}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186610528 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a274896-90a4-56a0-b45a-65385719edf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\left(-8 - \\pi\\right)}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a274896-90a4-56a0-b45a-65385719edf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\left(-8 - \\pi\\right)}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610520} :answer-field/id #uuid "3187eef1-7f80-587b-a0fe-39dc0cb198ff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610513}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "de532b59-dfad-573f-bd25-b6a82e67e141" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=- 3 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}$, if a curve $C$ is defined by the equation $y=x\\cdot f(x),$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}.$\n\nSlope $\\,=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=- 3 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\nu'(x)=1,\\quad v'(x)=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx} &=uv'(x)+vu'(x) \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(x)\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &{}+(- 3 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (1)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(x - 3)\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &{}+(- 3 x - 1)\\cdot (\\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\end{aligned}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left.\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}\\right|_{x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}} &=\\begin{aligned}&(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right))\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\right)} - 3 \\cos{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\right)}) \\\\ &{}+(- 3 \\sin{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\right)})\\cdot (1)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\cdot (- \\sqrt{2})+(- 2 \\sqrt{2})\\cdot (1) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\left(-8 - \\pi\\right)}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $\\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\left(-8 - \\pi\\right)}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613214 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "226e5c08-5e90-54e8-ba55-94ff70a2918d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612636} {:answer/id #uuid "622cc9e2-2ef6-5d02-946e-267a859ae820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612755} {:answer/id #uuid "77ac1ae1-a299-53b3-80df-b73c63f68172" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612792} {:answer/id #uuid "b6adf92e-cb25-50ee-a682-112f195d6fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612895} {:answer/id #uuid "ba0e5afd-7ee3-585d-8784-da4b915162f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6adf92e-cb25-50ee-a682-112f195d6fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612895} :answer-field/id #uuid "2947ec3e-35aa-5ec6-8ccf-8bea650fdaaf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613037}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f23ad49e-ef92-5ef1-81e1-83a5c66a2e4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-129328" :question/problem "Find $\\lim_{x\\to (-1,-1)}x\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=x\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nThe function $f(x,y)$ is continuous for all values of $x$ and $y.$ So, we can calculate the limit by substituting $(-1,-1)$ into the function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (-1,-1)}x\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+1} & =(-1)\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+1} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186615560 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a1e78ab-8788-5174-8ffd-7a2cc15b6e42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615555} {:answer/id #uuid "633cee45-d59f-53de-923d-085faddb4ddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615556} {:answer/id #uuid "7c1183b0-b75b-534f-9f78-973a4bb01276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615558} {:answer/id #uuid "cf15d09f-7e8e-5f63-801d-3da408b8e869" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615559} {:answer/id #uuid "f8866bcc-2a42-5656-b565-ee15147b562d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a1e78ab-8788-5174-8ffd-7a2cc15b6e42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615555} :answer-field/id #uuid "691ad0ef-2a57-5243-bdf1-ddb48cf7a828" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d5190bc4-2336-5db6-bb75-17e05e48e8ff" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(2 e^{x})\\cdot (x - 1)$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=0$." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=2 e^{x}$ and $v(x)=x - 1.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\nu'(x)=2 e^{x},\\quad v'(x)=1.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx} &=uv'(x)+vu'(x) \\\\ &=(2 e^{x})\\cdot (1)+(x - 1)\\cdot (2 e^{x}) \\\\ &=2 x e^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=0$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left.\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}\\right|_{x=0} &=\\begin{aligned}&(2 e^{(0)})\\cdot (1) \\\\ &{}+((0) - 1)\\cdot (2 e^{(0)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(2)\\cdot (1)+(-1)\\cdot (2) \\\\ &=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186619717 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05f02f53-47e0-53d0-947e-da99324e17ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619170} {:answer/id #uuid "1b644897-344d-5e88-b2d6-113f5842b131" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619204} {:answer/id #uuid "7f21646d-a333-5db7-8556-e9dcbfabf616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619367} {:answer/id #uuid "b3083031-33a5-5c24-adf2-0b1fe860dc66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619462} {:answer/id #uuid "b3460535-8260-548d-8c0f-54d97fa3e2b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3460535-8260-548d-8c0f-54d97fa3e2b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619463} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1418037-4648-56fe-b77f-4e1c6a90f9db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619705}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "08c91d6b-2f39-5f62-bcb1-ff8c61293232" :question/math-academy-id "q-27623" :question/problem "If $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ then $8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-2\\pi )+6=$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-1$ into the right-hand-side gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ then $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-2\\pi )=-\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-2\\pi )+6=8\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+6=-4+6=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186619728 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "213a4c1d-b52e-5221-8ad6-bafab66ca787" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619213} {:answer/id #uuid "34f2c4fa-9589-5f3b-a92d-7ab1dfecb4ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619254} {:answer/id #uuid "5e47ffcf-8937-546e-86c3-086790f1ca96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619313} {:answer/id #uuid "6ef1a6af-af24-5d21-9979-34303223d001" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619343} {:answer/id #uuid "b02b9187-1038-564f-a7c8-07dfab96ffd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e47ffcf-8937-546e-86c3-086790f1ca96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619313} :answer-field/id #uuid "48d39eb1-5500-5131-a5b1-8eba2c1dc701" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619626}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "28614a2a-126b-5809-92bc-8cfc91edc708" :question/math-academy-id "q-27012" :question/problem "Which of the following statements regarding the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ are true?\n\nI. The graph intersects the $x$-axis at $x=\\pi .$\n\nII. $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ has a minimum value at $x=\\pi$, which is equal to $-1.$\n\nIII. The range of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is $[-1,1].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. As $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=-1$, $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ does not intersect the $x$-axis at $x=\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a minimum at $x=\\pi$ and the value of the minimum is $-1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1]$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186621922 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23aac4b4-b610-59a8-be27-fd918324f000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621160} {:answer/id #uuid "a2e60e4c-71ae-56b9-acb7-5e2ebc0f7744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{csc}⁡y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621442} {:answer/id #uuid "b09cdb60-2a0b-51ae-9bbb-3b902a813122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{tan}⁡y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621476} {:answer/id #uuid "d1fae9a6-66b2-514b-9744-bcee7838151d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{tan}⁡y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621553} {:answer/id #uuid "efc3c9a7-b392-56db-8638-5d31be5c32b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{csc}⁡y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efc3c9a7-b392-56db-8638-5d31be5c32b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{csc}⁡y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621623} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfb97fe0-9d30-50c4-93f1-a473ca9caff2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621775}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e59005d4-fef2-529d-ab83-fbb5a84e31a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-2039" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 4\\operatorname{csc}⁡y\\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡y\\operatorname{cot}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡y+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4\\operatorname{csc}⁡y\\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =4\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡y\\operatorname{cot}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡y)+C \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{csc}⁡y+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186631884 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53da5106-e70d-5ad1-967f-be43ef65a87e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}+y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631359} {:answer/id #uuid "7641aae1-5cea-5e62-bc13-f69281245d5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-\\sqrt{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631428} {:answer/id #uuid "d18778e9-051b-5a37-9f69-e60c5f460fa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x-2{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631627} {:answer/id #uuid "d5125629-e1a8-53f9-90e9-35ff079d06bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}-2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631635} {:answer/id #uuid "d8e2477e-c358-5333-a3dd-60457a919cfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}^{2}-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8e2477e-c358-5333-a3dd-60457a919cfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}^{2}-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631646} :answer-field/id #uuid "48b618e3-2e1d-5898-8dd7-356068fbebc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "557300de-09b3-5e0a-8a2f-375395204316" :question/math-academy-id "q-69652" :question/problem "Calculate $det(M)$, if\n $$\n\\displaystyle M=\\begin{bmatrix}2x & \\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\sqrt{y} & -x\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2x & \\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\sqrt{y} & -x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot (-x)-\\sqrt{y}\\cdot \\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-y\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632064 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "267a0355-2f9b-591a-a5b7-f3122f078c98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{8}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632068} {:answer/id #uuid "284fdc57-cace-5ff2-b2e8-df45d06148e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632069} {:answer/id #uuid "2e73719e-1858-5ad9-b105-75906d9dc2a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{7}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632070} {:answer/id #uuid "96e019a9-8f39-5b51-b043-48a8a145a7c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{7}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632081} {:answer/id #uuid "bbfadeb9-5cb3-5120-b16c-a60acc2bbc47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{8}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "267a0355-2f9b-591a-a5b7-f3122f078c98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{8}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632068} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f051dfe-f49c-5b19-bcaf-65f74a79dd8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "21d74d11-27ac-56bf-bae4-d75f49dbc257" :question/problem "Calculate $F(x)$ given that $f(x)={x}^{7}$ and ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe apply the power rule with $n=7$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{7+1}}{7+1}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{8}}{8}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{8}}{8}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{8}}{8}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{8}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{8})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 8\\,{x}^{7} \\\\ &= {x}^{7}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22bcf2a9-77c7-5d82-b345-bdbb1e3f1ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{13}}{13}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632065} {:answer/id #uuid "305fca67-8c31-5139-bcad-b9fcdc295fe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{13}}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632071} {:answer/id #uuid "71071747-9658-5ec2-8413-923f0d38d0e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{12}}{13}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632077} {:answer/id #uuid "b086dc51-77e7-5eb2-891d-94c25c362f6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632086} {:answer/id #uuid "f146687b-9d31-527b-a2b2-004105d155ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{12}}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22bcf2a9-77c7-5d82-b345-bdbb1e3f1ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{13}}{13}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632065} :answer-field/id #uuid "687d9602-d083-5dde-849c-37c5281d7a0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2400a578-4e3e-50d6-aaa1-b71cd0eb4bcd" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int {x}^{12}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the power rule with $n=12$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int {x}^{12}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{12+1}}{12+1}+C=\\frac{{x}^{13}}{13}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{13}}{13}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{13}}{13}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{13}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{13})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{13}\\cdot 13{x}^{12} \\\\ &= {x}^{12}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632067 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "431270bd-146d-5112-b887-738a04648b51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{7}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632074} {:answer/id #uuid "851a58e8-4f4d-5e1e-baec-320b49fd6198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{7}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632079} {:answer/id #uuid "af29b014-c606-5fe0-a9dc-c8b52250806b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{6}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632085} {:answer/id #uuid "cf96ecc9-b2ab-5851-b199-ec857eeed39e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632089} {:answer/id #uuid "e47afe31-bd30-5b7b-8e1a-8407781f6103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{6}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af29b014-c606-5fe0-a9dc-c8b52250806b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{6}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632085} :answer-field/id #uuid "f160be36-0205-577c-a3ce-ed30257270ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "24a65f7f-6166-52b0-b66b-e7bb9af593bd" :question/problem "Calculate $F(x)$ given that $f(x)={x}^{5}$ and ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe apply the power rule with $n=5$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5+1}}{5+1}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{6}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{6})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 6\\,{x}^{5} \\\\ &= {x}^{5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632088 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09aece13-93fe-51d3-8a5d-b4a2ab7eb067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{21}}{20}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632063} {:answer/id #uuid "98f7e536-8b26-5303-9dc1-3a28e6569a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{20}}{21}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632082} {:answer/id #uuid "a280dfca-6b2b-56aa-9b48-fcaa1280329f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{20}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632083} {:answer/id #uuid "a4d0b5e0-9440-5979-a5ee-fc2cca5875bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{21}}{21}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632084} {:answer/id #uuid "f68f88e0-cb47-5014-b256-da46f2b718bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{20}}{20}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f68f88e0-cb47-5014-b256-da46f2b718bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{20}}{20}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632096} :answer-field/id #uuid "da6746a6-59ee-52ba-93e6-d5310d5500c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bd7041ea-d08b-5844-9b3c-40be8cd0bd12" :question/problem "Calculate $F(x)$ given that $f(x)={x}^{19}$ and ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe apply the power rule with $n=19$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{19}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{19+1}}{19+1}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{20}}{20}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{20}}{20}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{20}}{20}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{20}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{20})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{20}\\cdot 20\\,{x}^{19} \\\\ &= {x}^{19}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632091 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05e4247c-6054-5f84-84f5-ed5f824d5d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{5}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632062} {:answer/id #uuid "3bf81e1c-d2d5-5a7d-9e79-6d2e3e314f3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\fra